   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation to\npermitting village justices of the village of Maybrook to live in the towns of\nMontgomery or Hamptonburgh",
    "basePrintNo": "S4901",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4901-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3-300, Vil L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4901\n\nSPONSOR: ROLISON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation\nto permitting village justices of the village of Maybrook to live in the\ntowns of Montgomery or Hamptonburgh\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nPermits village justices of the village of Maybrook to live in the towns\nof Montgomery or Hamptonburgh.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Section 3-300 of the public officers law is amended by adding\nnew subdivision 33.\n\nSubdivision 33: In the Town of Maybrook in the County of Orange, the\nprovisions of this section requiring a person to be a resident of the\npolitical subdivision or municipal corporation of the state for which he\nor she shall be chosen or within which his or her official functions are\nrequired to be exercised, shall not prevent a person from holding the\noffice of village justice, provided that such person resides in the\ntowns of Montgomery or Hamptonburgh.\n\nSection 2. Section 3 of the public officers law is amended by adding\nanew subdivision 73.\n\nSubdivision 73: in the Town of Maybrook in the County of Orange, the\nprovisions of this section requiring a person to be a resident of the\npolitical subdivision or municipal corporation of the state for which he\nor she shall be chosen or within which his or her official functions are\nrequired to be exercised, shall not prevent a person from holding the\noffice of village justice, provided that such person resides in the\ntowns of Montgomery or Hamptonburgh. Provided, however, that the person\nperforming the function of village justice in any other village shall be\nfrom such village unless otherwise provided for in an act of the State\nLegislature.\n\nSection 3 states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAt the request of the Village of Maybrook, this legislation would permit\nvillage justice candidates to reside in the Town of Montgomery and the\nTown of Hamptonburgh. This change would aid in finding more candidates\nfor the position.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
